- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests`

**How to implement.** Publish calibration and Promote to library as semantic messages of the constructor window (001 §P `PublishCalibration`, `PromoteToLibrary`; 001 §I 'Revisions … "Publish calibration" writes the next revision', 'Promote to library mints the material's next version in the database'; .spec-md §4 'UI'). The arms call the Domain members (steps 406, 408) and record items through the kit as the Items panel does (step 240); the Publish step's buttons send them (step 418). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.5. In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: (1) `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains, each documented in one line: `PublishCalibration of FitRunName` (publish the run's item calibrations as the items' next revisions) and `PromoteToLibrary of FitRunName * PromotionSubject` (step 407). (2) Arms. Both go through step 185's read-only guard first. The run is the one of `kitFitRuns` of that name and its study the one of `kitStudies` the run names; a miss sets `kitStatus` to `The kit holds no fit run <name>.` and changes nothing. `PublishCalibration`: `study.calibratedItemsWith run model.kitItems` (step 406); `Error e` sets `kitStatus` to `Nothing was published — <e.describe>`; `Ok items` records each item, in order, through `{ kit = model.kit; imports = model.catalogueImports }.recordItem` (step 219), which snapshots its model and writes `<label>.item-json`, each recorded item replacing its old self in `kitItems`; all recorded, `kitStatus` is `Published the calibration of <the labels, comma-separated> from <the run's name>.`; the first write error stops it, the items recorded before it staying recorded (each item file is written whole, step 218), and `kitStatus` is `Not saved to the kit — <e.describe>`. `PromoteToLibrary (name, subject)`: for `MaterialPromotion version`, the entry `model.materials.resolveVersion version` answers (`Ok None` or `Error _` setting `kitStatus` to `The material version could not be read.`) and then `promoteMaterial study run version entry` (step 408); for `BlackBoxPromotion id`, the item of `kitItems` with that id and its `model.tryItemModelChoice` (step 263; a miss setting `kitStatus` to `The item or its model is not in the kit.`) and then `promoteBlackBox run item choice`; `Ok version` sets `kitStatus` to `Promoted to the library as <version.describe>.` and `Error e` to `Not promoted — <e.describe>`. Nothing else in the model changes: the library windows read the stores, and the member writes the kit's snapshot. No undo is added: publishing keeps every replaced value in the item's history (step 235), and promoting replaces nothing (step 408). No other message or option is added. Tests, in `StudyWindowModelTests`, over its kit with the study `QZ-LR` over E1 and E2 whose link makes CPL2's `c2.retardance` follow CPL1's (`StudyCommand (LinkParameters …)`), and a test-local fit run of it written through `writeFitRun` before the load, fitting CPL1's `c2.retardance` (`ItemOwner`) at 1.55 with σ 0.002, named `QZ-LR@20261101T120000Z`. `PublishCalibration records each calibrated item's next revision in the kit and tells which`: `PublishCalibration` of the run leaves `kitItems`' CPL1 and CPL2 at revision 2 holding that calibration, `readItems ()` answering them, and `kitStatus` `Published the calibration of CPL1, CPL2 from QZ-LR@20261101T120000Z.`. `a publish the run refuses, or of a fit run the kit lacks, is told and records nothing`: `PublishCalibration` of the same run again sets `kitStatus` containing `the calibration is already published`, and of a name the kit lacks `The kit holds no fit run`; `kitItems` and the item files are unchanged by either. `PromoteToLibrary of a fitted material mints its next library version and snapshots it into the kit`: with a user absorbing crystal material saved through the window's `materials` (as `StudyMessageTests` saves its own, step 366), opened by `QZ-LR` and fitted by a second run (`n1` at 1.7, `MaterialOwner`), `PromoteToLibrary (<that run>, MaterialPromotion <its version>)` sets `kitStatus` to `Promoted to the library as <the material's GUID> v2.`, `model.catalogueImports.proxy.tryHeldEnvelope` of version 2 holds `FitProvenance`, and the kit's `paths` hold `library/<the GUID>@v2.material-json`. `a read-only kit publishes and promotes nothing`: over the kit opened read-only, both messages are refused by the guard, and the folder's files and `tryHeldEntry` of the material are unchanged. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved.

**Acceptance.** After the publishing messages land, `PublishCalibration` MUST record every item a fit run calibrates at its next revision through `recordItem`, and `PromoteToLibrary` MUST promote a material or black box through `promoteMaterial` / `promoteBlackBox`, each telling its outcome in `kitStatus` and writing nothing under a read-only kit; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `PublishCalibration records each calibrated item's next revision in the kit and tells which`, `a publish the run refuses, or of a fit run the kit lacks, is told and records nothing`, `PromoteToLibrary of a fitted material mints its next library version and snapshots it into the kit` and `a read-only kit publishes and promotes nothing`, the count rising by 4; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the twenty s40 invariants MUST pass.
